What's your favorite thing about Matt?

00:10:28.760 --> 00:10:29.593
Leave a comment.

00:10:30.640 --> 00:10:32.610
- Isn't it funny how people
don't want to learn, though?

00:10:32.610 --> 00:10:33.910
To your point, they give this advice

00:10:33.910 --> 00:10:35.517
and then come up afterwards and be like,

00:10:35.517 --> 00:10:37.077
"So, what do I do now?"

00:10:37.077 --> 00:10:38.522
(laughing)

00:10:38.522 --> 00:10:39.410
- [Male] Go!

00:10:39.410 --> 00:10:41.100
- Well, learn, do.

00:10:41.100 --> 00:10:42.360
You can't just hire somebody,

00:10:42.360 --> 00:10:44.193
or at least that would be better.

00:10:45.410 --> 00:10:47.250
- [Male] Ask your mom, Google.

00:10:47.250 --> 00:10:49.568
- Google's your mom,
that was such a good--

00:10:49.568 --> 00:10:50.640
- Isn't it amazing how the
answers are all out there?

00:10:50.640 --> 00:10:53.620
There are no mysteries, people
don't want to accept that,

00:10:53.620 --> 00:10:54.970
that the answers are everywhere.

00:10:54.970 --> 00:10:58.480
- They don't want to do it,
it's no different than dieting.

00:10:58.480 --> 00:10:59.313
- Yeah, well.

00:10:59.313 --> 00:11:00.470
- They don't want to do it.

00:11:00.470 --> 00:11:01.950
- [Matt] Right, that's true.

00:11:01.950 --> 00:11:04.010
- [Male] So is that a lack
of intrinsic motivation?

00:11:04.010 --> 00:11:04.843
- I don't think so.

00:11:04.843 --> 00:11:07.490
- It's a disconnect
between words and actions.

00:11:07.490 --> 00:11:09.460
- Yeah, that's true, between
intention and action.

00:11:09.460 --> 00:11:11.850
- It's a disconnect between the narrative

00:11:11.850 --> 00:11:12.870
one is putting out to the world--

00:11:12.870 --> 00:11:15.333
- And back to themselves,
I really want this,

00:11:15.333 --> 00:11:16.732
but you really don't want it,

00:11:16.732 --> 00:11:18.320
because the information is available.

00:11:18.320 --> 00:11:20.097
- 100%, like I fuckin' really wanted it,

00:11:20.097 --> 00:11:22.633
and I gave up my fuckin' twenties.

00:11:24.430 --> 00:11:26.840
I can never, through all my passion,

00:11:26.840 --> 00:11:29.840
actually describe how
fucked up I played it.

00:11:29.840 --> 00:11:33.660
I mean it, I fucked up,
like it was too ridiculous.

00:11:33.660 --> 00:11:34.513
I did nothing.

00:11:35.660 --> 00:11:36.800
- [Matt] What do you mean?

00:11:36.800 --> 00:11:40.070
- I over corrected, I
worked every minute, 100%.

00:11:40.070 --> 00:11:42.550
- My brother's always giving
me shit, like you're gonna die.

00:11:42.550 --> 00:11:44.490
This is what it looks
like, it's on a scalpel.

00:11:44.490 --> 00:11:46.170
I gotta fuckin' over-correct to end up

00:11:46.170 --> 00:11:48.318
anywhere near where I want to go, right?

00:11:48.318 --> 00:11:51.867
And I might die in the
process, hopefully not.

00:11:51.867 --> 00:11:56.363
- But it's kind of like,
being a fuckin' caterpillar.

00:11:57.320 --> 00:11:59.723
I'm gonna be a fuckin' butterfly.

00:11:59.723 --> 00:12:03.490
This is the destiny,
nothing else is interesting.

00:12:03.490 --> 00:12:05.040
- [Matt] No, I agree,
well this is my hobby.

00:12:05.040 --> 00:12:09.190
- This, with death, is better
than not this without death.

00:12:09.190 --> 00:12:10.590
- Well I always say,
what's the alternative?

00:12:10.590 --> 00:12:11.490
This is a better outcome.

00:12:11.490 --> 00:12:12.773
- I'd rather live happy.

00:12:14.922 --> 00:12:17.800
(distant male mumbling)

00:12:17.800 --> 00:12:20.553
I'd rather be happy, going
from Columbus to New York.

00:12:20.553 --> 00:12:22.451
(laughing)

00:12:22.451 --> 00:12:25.690
(upbeat music)

00:12:25.690 --> 00:12:28.330
- [Camera Man] So we're waiting
here in the next location

00:12:28.330 --> 00:12:32.530
for the next meeting,
and Gary's just hidden

00:12:32.530 --> 00:12:37.530
behind some cars across
the street. (chuckles)

00:12:37.926 --> 00:12:39.010
I wonder if he can see us,

00:12:39.010 --> 00:12:40.590
'cause I feel like he just made a face.

00:12:40.590 --> 00:12:43.580
(laughing)

00:12:43.580 --> 00:12:44.663
I can't tell.

00:12:45.810 --> 00:12:48.080
- [Camera Man] This is a short
little segment in our episode

00:12:48.080 --> 00:12:49.880
that we like to call The Daily Rock.

00:12:51.290 --> 00:12:52.570
It's early in the
morning and we're walking

00:12:52.570 --> 00:12:54.130
through the hotel lobby.

00:12:54.130 --> 00:12:56.483
The Wild Rock looks a
little tired, doesn't he?

00:12:57.360 --> 00:13:00.060
A little bit on the sleepy
side, ladies and gentlemen.

00:13:00.920 --> 00:13:03.453
I really hope this makes
the DailyVee episode.

00:13:03.453 --> 00:13:06.194
(chuckles)

00:13:06.194 --> 00:13:08.409
If I'm editing it, it will.

00:13:08.409 --> 00:13:10.650
- The DailyVee and Daily Roo.

00:13:10.650 --> 00:13:12.730
- Oh, the Daily Roo?

00:13:12.730 --> 00:13:14.940
(chuckles)

00:13:14.940 --> 00:13:19.710
Notice The Rock in his wild
environment here, still has wit.

00:13:19.710 --> 00:13:21.559
Still has wit.

00:13:21.559 --> 00:13:23.297
- Can you not, please.

00:13:23.297 --> 00:13:24.373
You know you love it.

00:13:25.270 --> 00:13:26.557
- [DRrock] I'm not gonna
let you in the room,

00:13:26.557 --> 00:13:29.124
I'm just gonna let you
walk around the hallway.

00:13:29.124 --> 00:13:31.707
(upbeat music)

